                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "M.A.X. is a super cool game from my childhood. Back then, I spent countless hours playing it, and I recently rediscovered it on Steam (my CD is somewhere in the basement). Installation was quick and easy, and configuration and optimization were done in no time.\nWhat we already know: Strong strategic elements, including unit and building upgrades, and cool enemies. In my opinion, the graphics are still absolutely top-notch today and fit the game perfectly.\nA minor fix for crashes: The fan project “M.A.X. Port” replaces files and the engine, making the game playable even beyond 120–140 rounds and at higher resolutions. Saving and reloading still helps with minor glitches, though.\nCan I still recommend it today?—A resounding yes, for anyone who loves this genre.\nTested and played on Linux (Pop OS; default Steam Runtime 1.0; fan project) - run \"max-port\" in the terminal not from steam.",
